)
#index-end("Saviolo, Vincentio", "First ward")


===== Second Ward

#index-start("Saviolo, Vincentio", "Second ward")
Second, it starts from his 'second ward'#index("Guard", "Saviolo's second ward") which he describes as follows, somewhat contrary to the accompanying illustration (@saviolo_w2):

#set quote(block: true)
#quote(attribution: [#cite(
  <Saviolo_1595>,
  supplement: "17",
  form: "prose",
)])[[The scholler must] place his right legge formoste, a little bending the knee, so that the heele of his right foote stand just against the midst of his left foote, holding his swoord hand close on the outside of his right knee, with his swoorde helde in shorte, least his adversarye should gaine the same, ever keeping the poynte directlye on the face or bellye of his enemye]


#sourced-figure(
  image("../assets/Saviolo_2.jpg", width: 95%),
  caption: [Saviolo's second ward.],
  source: "https://wiktenauer.com/images/archive/3/3b/20130915232754%21Saviolo_2.jpg",
  tag: "saviolo_w2",
)

#index-end("Saviolo, Vincentio", "Second ward")

===== Third Ward

#index-start("Saviolo, Vincentio", "Third ward")
In contrast to the previous two wards, the description of the third ward (@saviolo_w3) is rather vague#index("Guard", "Saviolo's third ward").
First, he writes:

#set quote(block: true)
#quote(attribution: [#cite(
  <Saviolo_1595>,
  supplement: "19",
  form: "prose",
)])[... this third warde, which notwithstanding is quite contrarie to the other two. Because that in this you must stand with your feet even together, as if you were readie to sit down, and your rapier hand must bee within your knee, and your point against the face of your enemie]

And a few pages later:

#set quote(block: true)
#quote(attribution: [#cite(
  <Saviolo_1595>,
  supplement: "22",
  form: "prose",
)])[When you perfectlie understand your weapons, it maie serve you otherwise, so that you hold not your swoord hand within your knee, for if you finde your enemie to beare his swoord long, being in distance, you maie sodenlie beat it aside with your swoord]

#sourced-figure(
  image("../assets/Saviolo_3.jpg", width: 95%),
  caption: [Saviolo's third ward],
  source: "https://wiktenauer.com/images/archive/4/40/20130915232805%21Saviolo_3.jpg",
  tag: "saviolo_w3",
)
#index-end("Saviolo, Vincentio", "Third ward")
